[
{
  message: <<EOD
GNS3 server

The server runs as user "gns3" with HOME=%%VARBASE%%/db/gns3.  Its database,
projects, images and appliances live below that directory; logs go to
%%VARBASE%%/log/gns3.

Enable and start it:

  # sysrc gns3server_enable=YES
  # service gns3server start

The Web UI and API listen on http://127.0.0.1:3080 by default (API prefix
/v3, for example GET http://127.0.0.1:3080/v3/version).

Configuration lives in:

  %%ETCDIR%%/gns3_server.conf

The first start creates a default administrator (admin/admin) and a JWT
secret in %%VARBASE%%/db/gns3/GNS3/secrets.  Change the password right
after the first login.

Optional components
-------------------
- uBridge (required for Ethernet switches): net/ubridge.  For tighter
  security, restrict the setuid binary to the gns3 group:

    # chgrp gns3 %%PREFIX%%/bin/ubridge
    # chmod 4750 %%PREFIX%%/bin/ubridge

- Dynamips: emulators/dynamips-community
- QEMU: emulators/qemu (runs under TCG, there is no KVM on FreeBSD)
- VPCS: not available in the Ports tree; install it manually and set
  vpcs_path in the configuration file.

Unsupported node types on FreeBSD: Docker, VirtualBox, VMware, IOU/IOL and
the GNS3 VM.
EOD
}
]
